Alvea — Licensing

Copyright (c) 2026 Daishin

This repository is split-licensed. Different parts of the project are released
under different licenses:

  - Hardware design files and documentation
    (schematics, PCB layout, BOM, DESIGN.md, README.md, images, and all other
    non-firmware contents)
      → Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International
        (CC BY-NC 4.0). See LICENSE-HARDWARE below in this file.

  - Firmware
    (ZMK keymap, board/shield definition, and any other code intended to run
    on the device — typically under a `firmware/` or `config/` directory)
      → MIT License. See LICENSE-FIRMWARE.

Rationale: the firmware is built on and distributed with ZMK, which is
MIT-licensed. Matching ZMK's MIT license keeps the firmware compatible with
the ZMK ecosystem and free of licensing friction. The non-commercial
restriction that protects this project from being sold as a product applies to
the hardware design — the layer someone would actually manufacture.

If any file's license is unclear, the license in the nearest LICENSE file
(or an SPDX header in the file itself) takes precedence over this summary.

